22K likes, 240 comments - chrisburkard on October 8, 2026: "Oregon Coast Trail … by bike. Days 1&2 we travelled ~100 miles from Astoria to Tierra Del Mar. Despite a flat tire within the first 5 minutes, the start of our journey down the Oregon Coast has been even more wild than expected. We paddled by Packraft & ferries across a few beautiful rivers, some felt intense & remote, others were comfortably close to some cozy beach cabins. We’ve taken hiker ferry services across a few busier harbors. The people we’ve met have been amazing. Friendly and helpful, most of them very stoked on the crab & salmon season they’re having. The tides though have presented some challenges. With some bigger and more remote crossings to come, this impact will likely be intensified by the 8.0 ft tides on the forecast. But it looks like we have a pretty clear weather window ahead and are feeling good for the next 264 miles!
@astraldesigns @traveloregon 

📸: @masoncasey @shredskyy".

